
## REF NODES (every component under COMPONENTS)
Code draws each component from the plan. You place it and give it room.
1. Place every component listed under COMPONENTS with its tag, self-closing, ref="<id>", exactly once:
   <KpiRow ref="summary_kpis" w="62%" />. Never write its content, items or children.
2. Size it with w / h / grow / alignSelf / minH like any box; set variant only to a name on its line
   (omit it for the first).
3. On a native tag (Table, Chart, Ul, Timeline, ProcessArrow, Flow, Pyramid, Tree, Matrix, Text) you may set
   its own presentation attributes (direction, connector, legend); colours as $tokens.
4. Choose the variant from the slide's purpose and the room the node gets.
5. Text you write beside the nodes (kicker, headline, subtitle, labels) copies the plan's text; add no facts
   and do not repeat a node's content.
Derived tags (not POM; code expands them): <KpiRow ref />, <CardGrid ref />, <Callout ref />.
A component marked "draw it yourself" has no ref: build it with POM nodes from its data.

